    {
      "id": "glyph-template-content",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Content",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1300,
        "y": -560
      },
      "width": 460,
      "height": 280,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "glyph-template",
          "nodeId": "glyph-template-content"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:28px;background:#ffffff;font-family:system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow:auto'><h1 style='margin:0 0 12px;font:800 24px/1.2 system-ui'>Glyph</h1><p style='margin:0 0 12px;max-width:62ch;font:400 15px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'>A Glyph is the single port a Surface's chain ends on -- not a stop the chain passes through on its way somewhere else, but what the chain resolves to. It carries no further relationship of its own: once a chain reaches a Glyph, there's nowhere else for it to go.</p><p style='margin:0;max-width:62ch;font:400 15px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'>This template's own Glyph (the AccountTree icon, off to the right) plays both roles at once: it's the primitive this graph exists to demonstrate, and it's also the terminal node of this template's own Detail -> Icon -> Glyph chain -- the same node serving as subject and conclusion.</p></div>"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791306057406,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    }
